Requirements
• Experience in Project Management, Technology Consulting, Project Coordination or a similar role;
• Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;
• Genuine curiosity and enthusiasm for AI and technology;
• Confidence interacting with clients, partners and technical teams;
• Comfortable presenting, facilitating discussions and bringing people together;
• Strong organization, ownership and follow-through;
• Ability to understand business problems and translate them into concrete actions;
• Fluency in Portuguese and English.
Nice to have
• Exposure to AI, digital transformation or technology innovation projects;
• Experience working directly with companies or external partners;
• Experience with workshops, presentations, events or technology communities;
• Familiarity with generative AI tools and current AI use cases;
• Basic understanding of APIs, cloud environments, integrations or technology infrastructure;
• Experience with Jira, Linear or similar tools.
Benefits
• Hybrid Work: 3 days per week on-site in Tomar;
• Opportunity to work on AI, technology and innovation initiatives;
• Exposure to different businesses, projects and stakeholders;
• Opportunity to participate in workshops, events and technology initiatives;
• International projects and clients;
• Supportive and collaborative environment;
• Long-term contract.

Join us as a Backend Department Lead and drive the technical direction and development of the backend platform behind one of the fastest-growing AI products in the US market. 

We are looking for a strong technical leader who combines deep expertise in high-load system architecture with hands-on engineering leadership and experience in building and developing high-performing backend teams. In this role, you will have real technical ownership of our AI Gateway, generative pipelines, and mission-critical backend services powering a product already used by more than 2 million people.

About Us:
Zeely is the agentic AI platform for creating, launching, and scaling paid ads.

Simply put: we've made the best AI solutions and marketing tools available to small and medium businesses — tools that used to be reserved for big brands with expensive marketing teams.

The next big step: a B2B solution for large marketing teams and enterprise clients — workflows, creative analytics, and full control over campaigns across the whole team. For companies where performance marketing already runs at scale and needs more efficiency and automation.

A few numbers that speak for themselves:

 - 4 years on the market — a stable, profitable company backed by international investors;

 - 6× growth over the past year;

 - 2,000,000+ businesses already use Zeely;

 - #1 in its category in the US market;

 - 200+ specialists on the team;

 - Markets: US + worldwide.

Your Key Responsibilities:

 - Lead the Backend Department and set the technical direction for a team of 15+ backend engineers;

 - Own backend architecture and drive key technical decisions around scalability, reliability, performance, and system design;

 - Lead the evolution of our AI Gateway — the core platform layer powering text, image, voice, avatar, and video generation across multiple AI models and providers;

 - Design and evolve AI orchestration pipelines, optimizing routing, fallback strategies, generation quality, latency, and cost;

 - Scale backend services and infrastructure to support growing product traffic and increasingly complex workloads;

 - Drive engineering excellence across code quality, architecture, security, observability, testing, and operational reliability;

 - Lead strategic backend and AI initiatives, including our proprietary RAG pipeline, MCP integrations, and AI agent capabilities;

 - Stay hands-on with architecture, design reviews, code reviews, troubleshooting, and technically complex initiatives;

 - Grow the backend team through mentoring, performance management, technical development, hiring, and strong engineering practices;

 - Collaborate closely with Frontend, Mobile, QA, AI Engineering, DevOps, and Product teams to translate business goals into scalable technical solutions;

 - Partner with the Principal Engineer on infrastructure strategy, capacity planning, reliability, and cost optimization.

What We Are Looking For:

 - 7+ years of commercial backend development experience with Node.js;

 - 3+ years in a technical leadership role such as Backend Lead, Team Lead, or Engineering Lead;

 - Experience leading and developing backend engineers, including mentoring and performance management;

 - 3+ years of hands-on production experience with NestJS;

 - Strong system design skills and proven experience designing and evolving microservice and distributed architectures;

 - Experience building and scaling high-load production systems;

 - Deep expertise in PostgreSQL and Redis, including performance optimization, data modeling, and caching strategies;

 - Experience with ORMs such as Prisma and Drizzle;

 - Hands-on experience with AWS, including EKS, RDS, SQS, S3, CloudWatch, and OpenSearch;

 - Strong practical knowledge of Docker and containerized environments;

 - Strong understanding of reliability, observability, monitoring, incident management, and on-call practices;

 - Ability to balance architectural strategy with hands-on engineering and pragmatic delivery;

 - Upper-Intermediate English or higher.

Nice To Have:

 - Active AWS Solutions Architect or Developer certification;

 - Experience with Terraform or other Infrastructure as Code tools;

 - Experience optimizing infrastructure and architecture for cost, latency, and performance at scale;

 - Payment systems integration experience;

 - Backend experience across both mobile applications and web products;

 - Experience with GCP and Cloudflare;

 - Experience hiring and scaling engineering teams in fast-growing product companies.

AI Expertise We Value:

 - Commercial experience integrating AI APIs such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, or other model providers;

 - Experience designing multi-model orchestration systems, including routing, fallbacks, retries, rate limits, and cost/latency optimization;

 - Understanding of production challenges around AI workloads, including reliability, observability, and provider dependencies;

 - Experience with AI-assisted engineering and code review tools such as Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, or similar;

 - Understanding of RAG, embeddings, vector search, MCP, and AI agents;

 - Hands-on production experience is a strong plus.

Why it’s exciting to work with us:

 - Take technical ownership of the backend platform behind a rapidly scaling AI product;

 - Shape architecture and engineering standards across a strong backend organization;

 - Work on real production challenges around high-load systems, AI orchestration, distributed architecture, and infrastructure at scale;

 - Build with cutting-edge AI technologies and directly influence how they are integrated into the product;

 - Join a strong engineering team with significant autonomy and direct impact on product and technical decisions;

 - Remote-first approach: work from anywhere, with the option to visit our offices in Warsaw and Kyiv;

 - Regular performance reviews with transparent growth and compensation discussions.

